"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[19470],{319470:e=>{e.exports="---\nname: model-serving\ndescription: |\n  MLflow model logging, Unity Catalog registration, and registered-model discovery/loading. Use when\n  (1) logging models to Unity Catalog with MLflow, (2) the user needs to include signature and\n  input_example in log_model calls, (3) logging HuggingFace transformers models with\n  mlflow.transformers, (4) logging custom PyFunc models, or (5) listing registered models in a UC\n  schema or loading a registered model by alias/version. Covers classical ML, HuggingFace\n  transformers, custom PyFunc, GenAI agents, and UC model registry operations. Do NOT use for\n  model training or EDA — use the machine-learning skill instead.\n---\n\n# Model Serving\n\nLog MLflow models to Unity Catalog and deploy them to scalable REST API endpoints on Databricks.\n\n> **Note:** If there is any contradiction between the user's explicit preferences or instructions and the guidance in this skill, always defer to the user's preferences.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- Logging models to Unity Catalog with proper signatures and input examples\n- Deploying MLflow models (classical ML or custom PyFunc) to serving endpoints\n- Working with HuggingFace transformers and MLflow\n- Listing registered models in a Unity Catalog schema\n- Loading a registered model by alias or version\n\nDo NOT use this skill for model training or EDA — use the `machine-learning` skill instead.\n\n## Quick Decision: What Are You Doing?\n\n| Task                                              | Pattern                                                   | Reference                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Log traditional ML** (sklearn, xgboost)         | `mlflow.sklearn.autolog()` or manual `log_model`          | [logging-registration.md](logging-registration.md)   |\n| **Log HuggingFace Transformers**                  | Wrap in `pipeline()` then `mlflow.transformers.log_model` | [logging-registration.md](logging-registration.md)   |\n| **Log a custom Python model**                     | `mlflow.pyfunc.PythonModel` + `log_model`                 | [logging-registration.md](logging-registration.md)   |\n| **Log a GenAI Agent** (LangGraph, tool-calling)   | `mlflow.pyfunc.log_model` with file-based agent           | [logging-registration.md](logging-registration.md)   |\n| **List registered models in a UC schema**         | SDK (recommended) or paginated `MlflowClient`             | [uc-registry-discovery.md](uc-registry-discovery.md) |\n| **Load a registered model (by alias or version)** | `mlflow.pyfunc.load_model(\"models:/<name>@<alias>\")`      | [uc-registry-discovery.md](uc-registry-discovery.md) |\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **ALWAYS include both `signature` and `input_example`** when logging models — required for Unity Catalog registration and serving endpoint compatibility.\n2. **ALWAYS wrap HuggingFace models in a `pipeline()`** before logging with `mlflow.transformers.log_model` — do not pass raw model objects.\n3. **Use `infer_signature()`** to automatically generate model signatures from sample data.\n"}}]);
